  "title": "Workshop Exchange",
  "rules": [
    "Each worker owns one complementary tool and workstation; one raw unit takes three or four ticks to become that type of component.",
    "Completed components stay on the owner collection shelf until physically collected.",
    "Post a component-for-next-type or component-for-raw offer; that exact component is removed into escrow.",
    "Adjacent buyers settle real handoffs using public rotating priority. Unsold offers return after eight ticks or cancellation.",
    "Depositing all four types starts a three-tick shared assembly with public contribution credit.",
    "A finished machine rewards everyone and its contributors. Private station sales pay immediately but consume scarce parts.",
    "Two machines naturally finish the episode; exhaustion and poor coordination remain possible."
  ],
